# bmcd is a cargo package: Buildroot fetches the GitHub archive, runs
# `cargo vendor`, and stores the re-packed archive (the "-cargo2" suffix)
# -- so the sum covers the vendored crates too, exactly as Buildroot does
# for its own cargo packages.
#
# THE SUM DEPENDS ON THE RUST TOOLCHAIN, not just on the commit. The
# archive is named after the commit alone, so a stale one in dl/ looks
# right and hashes wrong. Measured on 2026-09-08 against commit 9b5cffa:
# rust-bin 1.85.0 vendored
# 9815f9cb190773112439b8979222f45ee79124f15ace2d29c5484141be679f65,
# rust-bin 1.98.1 vendored
# 84b9825371b085cea0f21ef03efd50893cfb16c0806cecb98c3700d605b44b9c.
# Recompute after any Rust bump, from a tree re-extracted AFTER the bump --
# buildroot_patches/ are applied at extract time, so a tree extracted
# before the patch changed still carries the old toolchain and produces the
# old sum under a name that looks correct.
#
# Computed with buildroot/local.mk REMOVED. A dev override rsyncs a working
# tree instead of downloading the pinned archive, so a hash computed with one
# in place would describe whatever happened to be on the workstation.
#
# The version is commit 8d1e734 on excavador-turing/bmcd branch `hive`,
# released as v2.36.3. Two fixes:
#
#   2.36.2  a session this daemon issues is one it will take back. OpenSSL
#           refuses to resume a session on a server that asks for client
#           certificates unless the context carries a session id context, and
#           the refusal is a FATAL internal_error, not a cache miss. A third
#           of all new connections from the fleet gateway died that way.
#           `load_tls_config` now sets one, derived from the client CA.
#
#   2.36.3  /metrics says which module is armed for USB boot, so a module
#           left in flash mode stops being indistinguishable from dead
#           hardware.
#
# The first of these changes a listener. It adds a call on the acceptor built
# in `load_tls_config`; it does not move the certificate, the client CA, the
# protocol versions or the cipher list.
#
# Measured 2026-09-12 with rust-bin 1.98.1 in the pinned container, from a
# tree with no buildroot/local.mk: `make bmcd-source` reported the sum below
# against a zeroed expectation, then re-run to confirm it fetches and
# verifies cleanly.
# v2.37.0 -> v2.38.0 (ebed91fa). Two additions, both from one Discord report
# on 2026-09-21 -- a user on a 2.4 board who had set the Split layout up and
# then had to give the BMC a fixed address over SSH, after which his clock
# said NOT synchronised and `chronyc sources` was empty.
#
#   The board's own address: GET/PUT /api/bmc/network/address, plus confirm,
#   revert, validate and limits. Applied on a bridge that is never brought
#   down (ifdown br0 would take the modules' ports with it), kept only when
#   a confirmation reaches the daemon AT THE NEW ADDRESS, reverted otherwise;
#   a confirmation from the board itself is refused. Only a confirmed
#   document reaches /etc/network/interfaces, as the v2.1 stanza the image
#   ships and S00dsa migrates. The daemon refuses what could never be
#   reached and warns about what is merely unwise -- no resolver being the
#   one that bit the reporter.
#
#   GET ?type=ntp carries chrony's verdict on every source: selected,
#   combined, excluded, unreachable, falseticker, too_variable -- and, when
#   chrony has nothing at all, the configured names as `unresolved`, which
#   is what "no resolver" looks like from the outside.
#
# Proved on board B with a local image before this pin: static apply and
# confirm from the new address, DHCP apply with the confirm refused from the
# board's own shell and the address put back on silence, then DHCP applied
# and confirmed; udhcpc stopped and started; the file written only on confirm.
#
# Measured 2026-09-21 with the pinned container, from a worktree with no
# buildroot/local.mk: `make bmcd-source` reported got 66f388b6 against a
# zeroed expectation.
sha256  66f388b6880bb831e382c3d5d62403b0ef6dceec3e753f7545a8fe7848c76c48  bmcd-ebed91fa93890a02592f1eb3607c47bb4049f27c-cargo2.tar.gz
sha256  809fa1ed21450f59827d1e9aec720bbc4b687434fa22283c6cb5dd82a47ab9c0  LICENSE
